def add(id,ids,scope,notes):v.append(ev(id,['night:'+x if x.startswith('P') else 'maps:src:'+x for x in ids],scope,notes))
add('V-D-001',['F.2.5','P1.1','P1.3'],'Integral matrices, affine caps and fundamental group','Read the complete supplied proofs. Recomputed A and B orders, the transposed marked monodromies, N^2=0 with rank three and primitive image, the fixed and coinvariant Smith groups, finite norm and cap freeness. The cap relations 5a=h, 4b=-h, a+b=0 have determinant one after elimination. The independent exact matrix replay is recorded separately.')
v.append(ev('V-D-002',['mapsaudit:order-four-torsion-transgression','maps:src:F.2.6'],'Integral order-four torsion transgression and 3-connectedness','Read the complete proofs, retaining the primitive boundary vectors e_theta=(1,0), e_h=(-4,1). For the order-four torsion coinvariant w, pullback is (w,0)->(w,-Norm(w))=(w,0), so the actual Cech boundary hits the global Z/2 generator with coefficient one. Recomputed the integral Leray filtration and used UCT/Hurewicz only after H2 and H3 vanished. The Uses edge from the torsion lemma is to F.2.5; F.2.6 uses the lemma.'))
add('V-D-003',['P1.4','P1.5','P1.7','P1.8','P1.9','F.3.5','F.3.6','F.3.7'],'Genus-two source, integral primitive/quotient comparison and lifted period plane','Re-derived the discriminant lambda^15(3125lambda+256), node and zero/infinity root substitutions. The map from the primitive exterior square to its quotient has determinant two; its rational extension is an isomorphism, while the integral determinant and content obstruction are retained. The rank-three plane is the image of ell wedge H_dR, whose injection is u tensor[v] -> u wedge v; the rank-two Hodge domain instead has rank-one image. The splitting cohomology vanishes by the displayed orbifold floor computation, and the invariant-line displacement is transverse exactly where h+Im(xi) is nonzero.')
add('V-D-004',['P1.10','P1.11','P1.12','P1.13','F.4.1'],'Characteristic numbers and oriented diffeomorphism type','Re-derived c4=6, Todd=(3c2^2-6)/720, signature=2 mod 16 and |signature|<=4, hence signature=2, c2^2=2 and the odd form I3,1. The characteristic vector p1/2 has square two and odd coordinates. Reflection in (1,1,1,1), followed by sign changes, strictly decreases its positive fourth coordinate until it reaches one. The explicit map (a,b)->(a-b,-2(a+b)) proves that Euler and p1 determine the unstable normal clutching datum. The opened Wall extended-form theorem gives an almost diffeomorphism, and the opened Kramer-Stolz theorem absorbs the homotopy sphere in one HP2 summand; signature fixes orientation.')
add('V-D-005',['P1.15','P1.16','P1.18'],'Normalized connection, splitting, exact minimum and parameter domain','Read the complete source connection and certificate proofs. Derived the polynomial de Rham reduction identity, residue pairing, invariant vector, the 625*pi*i/128 normalization from the displayed residue vector, and the one-dimensional splitting quotient. Read each interval-bound partition and exhaustiveness argument; the five unchanged certificate programs were rerun under python-flint 0.9.0, with output JSONs byte-identical to cp25. These certify the unique minimum at lambda=infinity and hence the stated open half-plane; computational scope is separately recorded.')
add('V-D-006',['P1A.1','P1A.2','P1A.3','P1A.4','P1.17'],'Cohomology, tangent deformation, automorphisms and parameter injectivity','Read and re-derived the effective orbifold line, Hodge pushforwards, canonical class and Hodge table. The cusp normalization has the actual toric Cech complex; Grauert is used only after constant fibre cohomology is established. Recomputed the residue determinant and excluded its unique rank jump using the certified parameter bound. The actual one-parameter Kodaira-Spencer class spans H1(T), so its inverse function map identifies the Kuranishi germ including nilpotents. The centralizer is Q*I; the finite cap norm excludes -I. The translation exact sequence yields C times Z/2, with the displayed half-period checked modulo the lattice and through the primitive cusp.')
add('V-D-007',['P1A.5','P1A.6'],'No boundary endpoint and filling of punctured-disc families','Read the full endpoint arguments, including properness and Hausdorffness, normalization/resolution of the total space, discreteness of critical values, the intrinsic anticanonical base, and the application of the opened torus deformation theorem. Continuation of the marked periods contradicts transversality at a claimed boundary fibre. For a punctured disc, the Cayley transform extends the bounded half-plane parameter into the interior; a degree-two cover kills the finite translation torsor and H1 of the additive sheaf vanishes on the disc.')
add('V-D-008',['F.1.1','F.1.4','F.2.1','F.2.2','F.2.3','F.3.1','F.3.2','P1B.1','P1B.2'],'Preliminary integral and cyclotomic restrictions','Read the complete proofs. Recomputed the Kuhn cell Euler count 6d, fixed-point obstruction when I-A is invertible, primitive square-zero cusp normal form, parity/local fixed-rank restrictions and the integral cyclotomic enumeration. The blowup counterexample preserves the peripherals while adding even-dimensional homology, proving why the marked cap and cusp filling data enter the classifier.')
add('V-D-009',['F.2.7','F.2.8','F.2.9','F.2.10','F.2.11','F.2.12','F.2.13','F.2.14'],'Further finite spectra and integral 3-primary obstructions','Read every proof through F.2.14. Re-derived the orbifold group obstruction, the order-two fixed-subspace argument, a=1,b=0 and irreducibility. Preserved the full primitive-exterior-square Sp4->SO5 bridge before the rank-one-difference exclusion, and the cusp restriction map determining the unique nontrivial rational extension. Checked the 3-adic lattice-uniqueness argument, the displayed cap period maps and the Leray groups yielding the residual 3-primary torsion. The spectral list follows from the exterior-square Euler bound and the local fixed dimensions. The source matrix computations beyond the independent replay list are algebraic derivations, not claimed additional program executions.')
add('V-D-010',['F.3.4','F.3.8','F.3.10','F.3.11'],'Polarized source obstruction and the relative period construction','Read and re-derived the semisimplicity/parity obstruction using the opened Deligne theorem, the nine explicit skew and rank-two symmetric spray directions with determinant -16, and the lower singular-value bound for I+sA. Read the relative Cartan-A/finite-jet gluing argument and the bounded cusp graph construction; no Serre-fibration property is assumed at the special fibre. Primary Oka input locators are recorded separately.')
add('V-D-011',['F.2.36','F.2.37','F.2.39'],'Centralizer algebra reduction, canonical representative and classifier synthesis','Read the complete arguments. Checked the faithful three-dimensional action of the semisimple centralizer quotient, the resulting degree-at-most-three/matrix-factor list, and the principal ideal formulation. The least-height, then lexicographic representative terminates because the original matrix is in the enumeration; its displayed bound is in terms of the input height, not a universal finite box. The stated synthesis uses the complete marked chain, cap and cusp data. The external principal-ideal decider still requires its separately recorded opened-reference check; this event does not claim to reproduce that external algorithm.')
v.append(ev('V-C-001',['maps:src:F.2.5','night:P1.1','night:P1.3','night:P1.4','night:P1.8','night:P1A.1','night:P1A.2','night:P1A.3','night:P1A.4'],'Independent exact linear algebra, intersection and period checks','The standalone SymPy calculation passed all assertions. Initial runs exposed symbolic-expression equality and JSON serialization issues in the new audit code; both were repaired, then the exact assertion run completed with no failed mathematical test.',typ='C',verdict='pass',artifacts=['code/V/audit_fourfold_linear.py','code/V/audit_fourfold_linear.json','code/V/audit_fourfold_linear.stdout.txt']))
v.append(ev('V-C-002',['night:P1.15','night:P1.16','night:P1.18'],'Current interval-certificate replay','Installed python-flint 0.9.0 and reran certified_lift_bound.py, certified_minimum_root.py, certified_minimum_cusp.py, certified_minimum_cusp_annulus.py and certified_minimum_collar.py from unchanged cp25 copies. All five exited zero; all five certificate JSON files agree byte-for-byte with cp25. The omitted historical tuple module was reconstructed literally from the printed input matrices and is expressly marked as such. Infinity root: 900 accepted rectangles; zero root: 463; cusp annulus: 7033; collar: 117 with 427 continuation steps. The local Hessian and positive polynomial discs complete the covering proof.',typ='C',verdict='pass',artifacts=['code/V/replay/source_manifest.json','code/V/replay/code/part1','code/V/background/data/fourfold_tuple.py']))
iv=[ev('IV-D-001',['night:P3K.68','night:P3K.69'],'Physical-line duality, oriented cap comparison and fixed-edge flop','Read both complete proofs and re-derived the Hermitian fibre map D_M(e^{i theta}v)=e^{-i theta}D_M(v), the SU2-equivariant quaternionic intertwiner (a,b)->(bar b,-bar a), the physical/dual Hopf orientation, the order of the two cap products, inverse-map collar cancellation, and A_M=-A_U. The dual pair (-3H,-24chi) becomes the physical pair (3H,24chi); the native free pair is unchanged and its right integer is 6A_M. The actual Cox conjugacy adds that right integer to the central coordinate, giving 7A_M. The notation -D4 is explicitly an oppositely oriented ball, not the antipodal map.'),ev('IV-D-002',['night:P3K.72','night:P3K.73','night:P3K.74'],'Scalar vertical seed, complete fan transport and exact counterexamples','Re-derived the literal source and unit maps Z_n=Z,V_n=Z^{-n}V,h_n=hB^n,B_n=B; the physical vertical pair is (3H-3Jn(n-1),24chi). Substituted both fan generators into the target prism equations and checked uniqueness of their rational solution; integrality comes from the transported geometric classes. The original actual shorter loop has J=2 and class -2 at T2, whereas its proposed S=1 polynomial is zero. OS45 has physical reference class 3, contradicting the old 25. The all-residue fan witness replay and independent target linear solves are separately recorded.'),ev('IV-D-003',['night:P3K.93'],'E7 source-infinity closed formula','Read the complete proof and re-derived the groupoid combination I_a(P)=-Z_a(P)-Z_a(JP)-C(P), its combined winding -8I, seed, generator identities S_prime=S+2D/w_i and D_prime/w2_prime=-D/w_i, and the displayed cubic prism entries. Substitution gives 1-a-3(a-1)(S-1)-(2a+1)(S-1)(S-3)/4. Writing S=2t+1 proves its period modulo 28 and the supplied matrices realize every listed residue. This source-infinity family is related to the scalar families only by the explicit four-boundary groupoid, so this formula does not restore the refuted scalar formula.'),ev('IV-C-001',['night:P3K.73','night:P3K.74'],'Current scalar all-fan replay','Reran the copied scalar_all_fans.py, source_all_fans.py and audit_scalar_all_fan_witnesses.py. The source manifest records the actual cp21 source paths and SHA256 values; the relevant scripts remained unchanged in the audited family. The run checked 39,024 bounded unimodular executions, 210 free-invariant cover checks, all 28 class witnesses and 86 independent target linear solves. This is a current replay, not the historical blind-control event.',typ='C',verdict='pass',artifacts=['code/IV/replay/source_manifest.json','code/IV/replay'])]
for p,a in [('IV',iv),('V',v)]:
 out=W/f'analysis/{p}/current_check_events.json';out.write_text(json.dumps(a,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
